@YLG I don’t think either one of them is any better or worse than the other. Yes, there’s a lot more focus on Hraustrekr, mostly because he’s a lot more directly antagonistic towards Jadis. However, the problems with Hraustrekr are also a lot more immediately visible.

Also, I highly doubt that Kestil would take a violent approach to trying to take the throne. It’s not his style. He would want some way of taking power that maintains his image. If he stages a coup and overthrows Hraustrekr, he’ll be seen as a tyrant, which would make maintaining control much more difficult. If he turns himself into the ‘savior’, then people will be happy to see him take over. It’s the same thing he’s been doing with Jadis. By villainizing his brother, then helping Jadis mitigate the damage of his actions, he’s made himself seem much more appealing. Sure, Jadis still doesn’t like him, but if she were forced to choose one or the other, right now, I think she’d choose Kestil. Her logic would basically be “sure, he’s a piece of shit, but at least he’s a piece of sh*t who’s helped me save lives, instead of standing aside while people die.”

All you need to do is look at the people Jadis surrounds herself with. Sev, Noll, and Vraekae are all in favor of Kestil, along with Eir’s family. On the other hand, I don’t think there’s a single person in Hraustrekr’s camp who she keeps around. The closest person to him who Jadis gets along with and actually talks to, willingly, is Wilhelm.

