@SeriousBlueJewel Alex can transfer about 1500 magic per hour. Plot-wise, that’s basically infinite magic. Enough for Jadis to cast infinite flight and mirror magnification, unlimited healing for Eir (she can heal more than 20000HP per 100 magic), and left some for Aila, Sorcha and Bridget. Jadis’ party just can’t utilise more magic. Well, Aila can, if she wants to level some city. Sorcha doesn’t even need Alex’s magic transfer, she can convert Eir’s healing to magic - that’s much more efficient. Once Sorcha creates some offensive wands, Sorcha/Eir or Sorcha/Sev combo would be devastating. With something like malediction dagger, but in form of a wand, they can kill demon princes easily. Hide in the shadows and suck HP from afar, the enemies won't even know what killed them.

Jadis totally can solo Vinea now. That worm had no chance to do anything against a super-fast flying target with the durability of a tank and the ability to penetrate any physical or magical defense. If other Demon Princes are anything like Vinea, I'd say Jadis can absolutely destroy them. Large, slow, defensive-type demons are ideal targets for Jadis's build. The ones that can give Jadis trouble are ranged casters with lightning or homing spells (like Dead Head Matriarch) or some kind of debuffers (paralysis, poison, illusion, curses etc.). Well, if the next Demon Prince uses lightning instead of earth magic, Jadis will have a hard time.

As for the Demon Lord, we don't know anything about him yet. Sure, he's smarter than some random Greater Demon or Matriarch, but is he "smart as f*ck"? He is more like Sauron-type of villain, a natural disaster that just exists. Such villains don't plot, they just send hordes and minions in the right direction, that's the limit of their intelligence. The Playwright is a smart and cunning villain. The Demon Lord is just... not dumb? He hasn't shown anything special yet, just basic common sense. As far as we know, he built walls around his base and sent the demons through the caves. Is that a genius level strategy? I’d say this is a level of 10y.o. kid who played RTS for dozen hours. He's probably dumber than Alex. Not much older, hasn't read any books, and has never interacted with smart people. He's probably... 3-4 y.o.? Spent most of his life in some edgy underground lair f*cking princes.

