@SeriousBlueJewel On a more serious note, I don't like the idea of slings for Jadis as regular issue. They do not fit her fighting style, take a lot of room to use and have a relatively long wind up time when compared to other ranged options.

The idea behind throwing knives is that they are small and compact. She can store them in a bandolier over her plate armor. Alternatively, she could easily carry a few pilum-like or javelin-like short throwing spears. Such weapons need less room to use and can be deployed much faster. They also synergize far better with her role as the main frontline tank and bruiser damage role. The most important reason to have them though, is so she can trigger her Mirrored Strikes even her bodies are separated.

If she never needed to do trigger it with a ranged attack landing just before the big melee blow, or if she couldn't trigger it with a ranged attack at all, then I would say she would have no need for any sort of ranged weapon at all.

